>Isn't the 4000 a CVAX processor?  It would be really nice to be able to run on
>the CVAX machines... IIRC in its last gasps that processor got up to about
>90 SPECint92.

The CVAX peaked at around 17 MHz, ~5 SPECint92.

The VAX SOC ("system on a chip"), used in the VAX 4000/VLC and VXT 2000,
is a CVAX + CFPU + 8KB cache on a single chip.  It got up to about 30
MHz.  The SOC is different enough from CVAX to need some minor porting
work.

The fastest VAX chips are NVAX, much different and running well over 100 MHz.

