says...
> In article <NmHHjAAqgf90Ewzx@dbslbox.demon.co.uk>,
> Dave Brettell  <Dave@dbslbox.demon.co.uk> wrote:
> >An old customer of mine has a PDP 11/23 running RSTS/E (god knows what
> >version).
> >They use a retail system written in un-compiled BASIC (both 2 and 4 word
> >versions - remember that back in the 70s ? - talk about LEGACY).
> >The code is dodgy at best - two digit year fields and dates are critical
> >(especially those before that magic year - how many seconds since 197
> >what not ?) ;-)
> >I changed the date on the PDP to the last day of December 1999 at 23:59
> >and watched it roll.   The best I can describe the result is watching a
> >random date generator at work (tip: - use your old PDP systems to
> >generate lottery numbers ).
