Well, if you come over to the PDP-11 specific newsgroups -
including comp.os.rsts, vmsnet.pdp-11, and alt.sys.pdp11 - you'll
find a fair number of people with -11's that are going to continue
running well into the 21st century.  The RT-11 and RSX-11M+ OS's
are now fully Year 2000 compliant, but I don't know about RSTS/E.

Of course, in an application such as yours where there's a huge amount
of date-dependent stuff in the application software, the OS compliance
is the easy end of the problem.

