>COBOL or whatever that will run on a Y2K compliant platform (any Y2K
>complient VAX systems about ?).

Open your eyes!  PDP-11's and VAXen are Y2K compliant platforms, with
the right software!

One very important question is whether the BASIC interpreter used
by your clients is available in a Y2K compliant version.  Which
version of RSTS/E BASIC are you using?  (Or BASICs, as the case may be.)

