In article <01bd422a$327797c0$b3451ed1@mikey.tenethealth.com>, "Mikey" <mikeyf_@_flash.net> writes:
>I have purchased a DECserver 90M network access server to connect to my
>DEChub 90 for the purpose of remote access to a VAX 4000-500A.  
>
>The first problem is that the 90M has no flashram in it, so I need software
>to load on it.  What software do I need, and how do I load it when I find
>it?  Is there a software package that will let me load the software on the
>90M from a PC using TCP/IP?

A DECserver 90M is AFAIK a DECserver 90TL with a slot for PCMCIA flash
memory and more memory (to run the Network Access Software, too). 

I think, you have two options:
- Obtain a PCMCIA flash memory and plug it in
- Boot via MOP or TFTP the MNENG1.SYS (standard DS90TL/DS90M) or
		the MNENG2.SYS (Network access software - DS90M only)
	(Note: the NAS software runs on DS900TM, too, the image is WWENG2.SYS)

>The second problem is that I am not totally sure how to connect the modems
>up to the 90M to get access.  What type of connection do I need between the
>modems and the 90M?  

The DECserver 90 have 8pin connectors with only 6pins used.
(TX, Rx, 2xGND, DSR, DTR). I think it should be enough for most modesm,
but perhaps not in their default configuration.

>I have a person that may be available to help me, but I would like to get
>some questions answered before I call him to save us some money.
>
>Thanks in advance for any help or references to someone that can help.
