:I'm looking for manuals for the DEC 433 WS, with APPIAN graphics card, SCSI
:Cabinet, 21 Inch VR320 - DA monitor.

  "DEC 433 WS"?  That might be a DIGITAL Personal Workstation, or
  it might be an older PC -- the presence of a VR320 monitor makes
  me think it's a fairly old IA32 Intel-based system.   You'll need
  to better identify which system it is.

:I Need general settings info, monitor capabilities, graphics settings.
:
:The monitor is fixed frequence. can't it run with Win95 and how?

  The VR320 is a 1280 x 1024 x 66 Hz display that was often sold in
  conjunction with the VAXstation SPX-series graphics controllers.

  There have been numerous questions asked in the past about older
  VR-series monitors.

  The basic answer is "forget it" -- but I know this answer runs
  counter to the "scrounge ethic".  :-)

:which other  Graphics cards can has been manufactured that fits in a PCI
:slot and can run together with 21" fixed freq. 72Hz monitor?

  Most commodity PC graphics controllers are incapable of working
  with the signalling used with the older VR monitors, as they are
  incapable of generating the required three-BNC RGB synch-on-green
  signalling -- most generate five-BNC RGB with seperate horizontal
  and vertical synchronization signals.

  Try a search for `synch and green' or whatever the appropriate
  syntax is in your favorite search engine, and particularly check
  the newsgroup archives at the http://www.dejanews.com/ site, and
  check the via various other archives around

  Also see the Fixed-Frequency FAQ:
    http://www.paranoia.com/~filipg/HTML/REPAIR/F_fix_freq.html

