Wow, cool.  I had no idea the Personal Dec had so much on it.  

: But I dont quite understand exactly what you're trying to do.

Here is the point of the project..  There is a lab with 24 Personal
DecStation 5000/(75??)s.  They can all create simple sine-wave
tones (the error bell for example).  

If a client ran multiple servers, one on each machine, and setting the
bell tone on each machine to a different frequency (..oh, say to a note in
a 2 octave musical scale) then the client could implement a polyphonic 
musical instrument across the range of computers in the laboratory.

Rather than at a high level setting the terminal bell configuration and
making a beep (through xset b <vol> <freq> <duration>), I want to do it at
a lower level that lets me make a beep on that machine when noone is
logged in through the X interface on the machine (I don't believe you can
make the computer create a simple tone unless you are logged into the
machine and have a localhost:0.0 connecton providing an interface for the
terminal bell to sound off).  If I'm wrong, please correct me.

This musical client is just an experiment really.  These computers
are rarely used (some of the slowest on my campus) and the concept
interests me quite a bit.  I guess you could think of it as a crude
electronic bell choir. ;]

