Miao Kaiji  <miaokj@public.east.cn.net> wrote:
>Hi:
>  I want to tranfer the data in VAX II system to pentium PC .

What operating systems?  If the VAX is running VMS, keep in mind
that many fancy file types available under VMS's RMS (indexed, most
notably) have no easy represnetation on operating systems that
don't have the fancy features of RMS.

>How can I do?

There are a number of ways:  TCP/IP, using FTP, NFS, or some other
protocol.  Tapes, assuming you've got media you can use on either
platform.  If you have none of the above, you can always install
recent versions of Columbia's Kermit on both machines and just send
the files over the serial lines.

If you don't know the answer to your simple questions, I'd highly
recommend that you find someone competent to organize the transfer
and pay them whatever they ask.  Computers are cheap; data is expensive!

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



