A friend of mine has a DEC PC loaded up with the usual consumer
bloat-ware, like WIN95 and "TeleCommander", which apparantly is the
application which enables the data-fax-voice modem to respond to
incomming phone calls, be they fax or voice.

Just as the WIN95 desktop appears (which takes about 3 times longer than
a "normal" P100 Mhz/72-MB RAM system), the following error appears with
an "OK" acknowledgement button:

"TeleCommander with WaveStream: One of the Software components required
for audio is not present or is an old version.  Run Setup to re-install
the audio drivers"

We are trying to figure out how to:
1) eliminate this error
2) prevent _all_ system-resource-hogging components of "TeleCommander"
from loading (he doesn't use this silly nonsense)
3) Maintain digitized sound (.VOC & .WAV) & FM Music capability
(currently all working)
4) improve the WIN95 desktop arrival time (relationship [if any] to the
"TeleCommander with WaveStream ..." error is unknown)

We notice:
1) WIN95 Device Manager under "sound, video & game controllers" contains
"Creative Labs Sound Blaster Pro" and NOTHING else, ie: No MPU401 or
gameport-joystick (un-usual I thought)
2) WIN95 Startup folder contains NO references to "TeleCommander" or 
"WaveStream"
