FreeBSD is, uh, "somewhat less portable" than NetBSD.  It's not likely that
you'll see it on the DECstation any time soon.

NetBSD performs pretty well on the 3100.  You might wait a week or so for the
NetBSD-1.3.1 release, which is a maintenance release of NetBSD-1.3.  Or
you could just install 1.3 now and upgrade to 1.3.1 later; that's easy.

NetBSD on the 3100 has Ultrix binary compatibility, so you should be able
to use your old programs.  And we've got X and all the usual goodies, plus a
fairly reasonable installation system.  Give it a try!

