Not to offend anyone, but if you start the FX!32 manager, press "Ctrl-C"
and a window named 'Schedule FX!32 Optimizations' will appear.
Under 'Global Actions' remove the marker in 'Make schedule active'.
This removes the schedule option, and from this point on, you don't need
to manually start optimizations anymore.
The apps that are waiting for the scheduler to start the optimizer, will
need
to be manually started, unless you start the app itself, and make the
profile
change more than the threshold setup for starting the optimizer(default
25%).

Regards, Anders Blicher Petersen





