In article <6cdupr$a18@usenet.srv.cis.pitt.edu>,
Gregg E Economou <geest3+@pitt.edu> wrote:
>
>hello,
>
>I recently acquired an HP1716 mag-op drive. 
>It is apparently working fine, but Ultrix will not recognize it as 
>a disk.
>in the firmware monitor, an inquiry of the scsi bus indicates that
>the device is considered to be of the type 'OPT' whereas disks are
>of type 'DIR' (direct access i assume) . Ultrix evidently doesnt consider
>this item to be a disk. 
>Is there any simple thing to do to get this thing working, or did i buy 
>a drive that wont work with ultrix? 
>hardware is a DS5000/200. 
>I havent found anything in the documentation available from HP on the drive
>about any kind of jumper or anythign to control how it reports itself
>to the host. 
>

I have a 1716T connected to an Alpha box running Digital Unix.  The jumper
you are looking for is not hardware, but rather a non-volatile RAM setting.
The basic information you need is contained in the HP manual entitled "Optical
Drive and Library, SCSI-2 Command Reference".  My copy says it is HP part 
number 5960-7606.

Page 2-23 has Table 2-17 "Inquiry Command Returned Data" for which byte 0
is shown as "Perhiperal Device Type (07H--Optical Memory(default); 00H--Direct
Access)".  Below the table is a Note to the effect that the value returned in
this field is dependent upon "the DAIR bit in the Vendor Unique Page 21H of the
Mode Select Command".  If the DAIR bit is 0, the device identifies as optical,
if 1, it identifies as direct access.

On pages 2-42 and 2-43, the DAIR bit is identified as the "Direct Access
Inquiry Response bit", with a value of 1 meaning indicated "Direct Access
Device".  The DAIR bit is the lsb of Byte 14(decimal, first byte being 0th) of
"Vendor Unique Page 21H".

It has been several years since I set this bit, but as I recall I used the 
"scu" utility to read/modify/write the parameter page.  I assume Ultrix has
some similar facility available. The relevant command codes are "Mode Sense"
(1AH) and "Mode Select"(15H).

Let me know if you need further information.
-- 
