On Wed, 18 Feb 1998, Marcus Daniel wrote:

Thank you for providing me with information about how to use a terminal as
console on a VAXstation 3100.

Of course, you were right :-) My only excuse is that I wasn'T able to
concentrate very well when I was trying to connect the terminal, due to the
late hour of the night.

Here's a little Summary for people having the same Problem and searching
some kind of news archive for an answer:

Terminal as console on a VAXstation 3100 :

- Push the tiny recessed switch next to the red 0-7 LEDs into the UP 
  position.

- Connect the serial line to the printer port on the VAX, maybe you have to
  use a null-modem adapter if your MMJ ("telephone jack") to 25pin
  connector is for modems/printers and not terminals.

- Use 9600 bps 8N1 vt100 as communication parameters for the terminal
  (terminal emulator program)

Here's the data, if you have to build your own cable :

MMJ (Vax)   -   RS232 DB25 (PC and such)

1 Rdy Out       20 DTR
2 TX+            2 TD
3 TX-            7 GND
4 RX-            7 GND
5 RX+            3 RD
6 Rdy In        6 & 8, 6 DSR, 8 DCD


Thanks again everybody for the prompt help on this, now I only have to get
around my netbooting problems :-) to make a unix box out of my vax.


Bye
       Marcus (danielm@uni-muenster.de)




