We have a Decnis doing a perfectly good job as a router.  Several 
ethernet segments attach to it, and it shuffles packets about between
them, and to the outside world.  It tells the outside world
via RIP which subnets it handles.

Now we want to hang some modems off a machine that is on one of
the ethernet subnets.  These modems are to have their own 
class C address.

We have the DECnis routing packets from the modems to all
the other subnets it personally knows.  We now want it
to advertise via RIP that it knows about this subnet.

How?

the subnet is not associated with a physical device, but with
a reachable address.  There doesn't seem to be any way to 
get the DECnis to add a subnet to its RIP tables unless that
subnet is associated with a physical port.  

Any clues?

