>
>   What sort of replacement disk device?  Manufacturer, model, etc?
>   How is it mounted.
>
>   I will assume that there is *no* associated disk device visible
>   with a SHOW DEVICE D.
>
>   Anything in the error log?
>
> :Yes, I've checked the SCSI jumpers on the drive and the connections
> :to the external chassis.
>
>   With no disk device visible, this is likely a result of a SCSI
>   connection problem (too long, bad cable, loose connection, etc)
>   a drive connection problem (ribbon cable, bent pin, etc), a
>   drive-internal problem (bad or no power, bad drive, etc), or a
>   SCSI unit number switch setting problem (wrong LUN, collides
>   with another disk or with the host controller LUN, etc).
>
>   Beware: I've seen some drives that have external switches that
