In article <34E6058C.811E2C84@ix.netcom.com>, Tony Robinson <adr76@ix.netcom.com> writes:
:I'm looking to check out a vaxstation 2000 - I have a vaxstation 2000
:box here that I need to plug into (vid out) and a keyboard, I take it
:needs a special keyboard and vid hookup - any suggestions out there in
:cyberspace, or a pointer to a web page?

  http://www.altavista.digital.com/
  ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/dec-faq/vms
    (including "VAX3.   Where can I find more info about VAX systems?")
  http://www.montagar.com/

  The VAXstation 2000 predates the "industry standard" commodity keyboard
  and video "standards", and is not compatible with them.  For a full test
  of the system hardware, yes, you will want to use the correct hardware
  and cabling.

  To see if the VAXstation 2000 passes self-test without having a graphics
  monitor attached, you can use a BCC08 cable -- the BCC08 was a serial
  cable that had a short between pins 8 and 9, and this short told the
  system that a serial console was present on the printer port.
 
