I think your estimates on the number of people it takes to do a
processor at dec are a little off. I'm pretty sure digital hasn't yet
had a project in the chip side that is several hundred people.  SA110
was <50.  I'm pretty sure that ev6 is less than 150 people.  So I
would say that it costs between 50-100M$ to design the cpus at dec.
Granted this is just a guess and I really don't have any information
that you don't have.  Compare this with the rumored number of people
on merced or katmai or willmette and its pretty incredible.  The basic
philosophy is put as few highly qualified people on a project as
possible.   


