> to this console mode.  Based upon my check of the Digital noname site,
> searches in Dejanews, and on the web, I have ARC installed (I think).
No, if you get a prompt (>> or >>> I suppose) it's the SRM console. If
your machine has both, you can type SET OS NT there and press Ctrl-P or
powercycle the system to get to ARC, IIRC. You also should be able to 
type HELP to get some help. SHOW DEV should show you a list of devices
and BOOT DKAx should boot from SCSI device x. The RedHat-CD is bootable,
so typing BOOT DKAx with x the ID of your CD-ROM should start the
installation. You'll have to look up "installing from SRM" in the manual
from RedHat if you want to try this. You can't have NT on the same drive
then, so I don't recomment installing from SRM if you really want to run
NT on your poor alpha :)

> ultimate goal is to load Windows NT and Red Hat Linux on it. 
Try to get on ARC console. Read the RedHat Manual for Alpha (it's on their
webserver). Connect to the RedHat/Alpha mailinglist if you run into real
problems...

