In article <6bsb2b$mr2$1@nnrp2.dejanews.com>, 
Dick.Cardwell@sgcs.co.uk writes:

> I have a problem booting a Microvax 3400 that we no longer have on contract.
> The machine is no longer actively used and I have been using it to test out
> upgrades etc. The console displays the following on the console following
> power on.
> ...
> 36..35.. etc
> Until it reaches 3 where it tells me that
> 
> Normal Operation Not Possible.

My manuals are across town right now, but I had a similar (if
not identical) problem.   A friend has rescued the system
from a dumpster after it was tossed out because of this
problem.

It turned out that the fuse for the DSSI bus was blown.   The
system would actually boot and run from an alternate (Emulex)
controller on the Q-Bus, but could not access the DSSI bus.

There are (as I recall) two tiny fuses ("Picofuses") on the CPU
board.   It would be worth checking both of them.   As I recall,
they are socketed, so testing and replacing them should be easy.

If this doesn't solve the problem, let me know and I will go
dig out the manuals.

Alan

