X-Deja-AN: 324309142
References: <1998Feb5.103142.1242@flying-disk.spamblock.com> <6bn920$kpc@usenet.pa.dec.com> <34DFB4CD.614@consentric.net> <1998Feb10.105241.1246@flying-disk.spamblock.com>
Organization: Flying Disk Systems, Inc.
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Well, I have done some more testing of the TLZ09 compatibility
problems.

Using the AlphaServer 1000A with the internal TLZ09, I wrote
two tapes.   Both were brand new, right out of the wrapper,
3M DDS-90 tapes.

Except for disabling compaction on the first tape and enabling
it on the second, they were identical.   I used VMS Backup
to write about 50 files containing roughly 500,000 blocks to
each tape.   I then took both tapes to my AlphaStation 200 with
the Archive 4322NP/4542NP drive.

The first (non-compacted) tape restored (using /Verify) with
no problems.

The second (compacted) tape would mount OK (displaying the
volume label) and Backup could list the header information
and first several files.   Then a hundred or so errors would
be logged and I got the operator message to Continue or Quit.

So, it appears that something about compaction has changed
between the TLZ07 and TLZ09.   We never had this problem
with compacted TLZ07 tapes.

Does anyone have any ideas about where I should proceed from
here?

Alan

