Hi Susan,

  For the life of me I can't figgure out why people are
saying FX!32 doesn't optimise automatically.  It does for
me.  I will say that it does so on a user defined schedual.
I was very impressed with FX!32 and I can see why the software
has won so many awards!  I have a Alpha XL366 2meg cache and
32 megs memory (ouch) with a 1 gig drive.  The FX!32 TRANSLATES
and OPTIMISES CPU instructions as it encounters them with
the various routines (code chunks) within an application.  Just
make sure you "visit" as many menu options as possible the first
time through (Although this is not critical).

On my 366 the first time through is similar in operational speed
to a Pentium 100  the second time through is similar (and sometimes
faster) that my Intel 300 MMX sitting along side.   I run NT Server
4.0 an all 6 of my machines (except for my Amiga ;-)  I use the
machine for rendering 3D in Lightwave and Softimage.  I do TV CMs
here in Japan.  The XL366 out proforms any other single processor
system I have.  The Pro200 Duel does out proform it but...

The only reasons I can think of for your slow operations are:

     * You're running applications while FX!32 is working.
     * You're running applications in virtual memory :(

...at least those are the first things to pop into mind.  I know
that's kinda simplistic but I hope it helps...


James D. Prentice
