It's good press for Alpha, but what I can't stand is the peecee press
and Digital's market droids spouting about the Alpha doing digital
effects for Titanic, and then praising WinNT in the next breath
without ever mentioning Linux.

The serious number crunching was done on a "Render Ranch" of 160
Alphas.  They got 80 Linux and 80 NT initially but switched to 120:40.

With Linux they had a problem with a floating-point handler which they
fixed in the source before starting out.

With NT they had problems due to slow NFS, no symbolic links,
inability to mount enough drives and of course they couldn't fix any
of them or port their in-house scripts and tools properly.  They tried
working around the problems by isolating the NT machines, using Samba,
buying lots of extra disk...

They also used SGIs running Irix and had problems with server crashes. 


Rob.



