:SCSI device.

  I remember first getting MicroVMS V1.0 (I'm dating myself here :-)
  going in a weird configuration using the VMBUVAX1 mechanism -- this
  mechanism was a version of VMB that pretended to be SYSBOOT.  When
  the VAXstation I console VMB loaded SYSBOOT off a supported device,
  it was really loading a new version of VMB, and the new version of
  VMB had the support to load the real SYSBOOT off a device that the
  console VMB did not contain support for...

  Basically, you'd need to have a supported boot device around, and
  use this to load a version of VMB that does have support for the
  new device.

  This approach is not for the faint of heart, and likely requires
  access to the OpenVMS VAX source listings CD-ROM set and to the
  Internals and Data Structures Manual (IDSM).  (The CD-ROM part
  number for OpenVMS VAX source listings is QB-001AB-E8 -- circa
  US$2K price.)

