susan wrote:
> 
> I have recently installed windows nt 4.0 on a lx motherboard with a
> 533mhz P8 cpu.  I have a gl-1000 video card (8mb), 4.5 cheetah scsi hard
> drive, and 64mbs of sdram (ECC).
> 
> At the moment, on a few applications, it appears to run slightly faster
> than my amd k6, 233mhz with 64 mbs of sdram, 3.2gb ide hard drive, and
> s3 virge video card...and on most applications, it seems to run slower.
> When I use the term applications, I mean: netscape, iexplorer, receiving
> and sending mail....all 32bit software...no native alpha applications.
> 
> When using fx32: it really slows down....I was told it would run as
> quick as a pentium pro 200...not a chance.

Make sure you are using FX!32 properly.  Not only do you have to run the
software under FX!32, but you have to tell FX!32 to optimize the
translated
binaries.  It may take you a couple passes to get everything sorted out.
It's definitely worth your time to investigate the optimization
proceedure,
as the performance improvement for non-native Alpha applications is
quite
substantial.  You may want to check out the AlphaNT mailing list.

http://dutlbcz.lr.tudelft.nl/alphant/

> Next week I am installing linux redhat 5.0. I hope this will prove to be
> quicker.

A friend of mine had linux on a 433 MHz machines and the performance was 
quite good.  As a side note, we've found the 533 MHz new machines to be
about
25% faster than the older 500MHz machines under Digital UNIX.  Whether
this is
due to the larger L3 cache (2mb instead of 1mb) or SDRAM I'm not quite
sure
yet.

Jeff



