:Can anyone confirm that a modem can be used with a uVAX3100?

  Modems work fine on most (all?) OpenVMS VAX systems with serial lines,
  and on most (all?) LAT and IP terminal servers.

  One must specifically determine if the host serial port (or terminal
  server port) in question has at least limited modem control support
  if one wishes to use hangup and other associaed modem-control signalling
  features.  (DECconnect MMJ "modular" serial lines, unfortunately, do not.) 
  In other words, you will need to identify which serial port you wish to
  use, and which specific "3100" series box. 

