: Uwe
I'm not saying that the processor doesn't improve performance on a
per clock basis.  Indeed, at the 40 spec int @ 600MHz figure for the 21264
the performance has obviously improved by a factor of two over the 21164.
I'm just wondering if they could have gained the additional 50% in
performance to get 40 spec int @ 400MHz that some people are saying,
especially since the emphasis with the Alpha is reducing cycle time
rather than creating super-braniac designs.  

Simply doubling the number of integer units isn't going to double
performance.  You still have to find ways to keep the units
busy, and that implies either better scheduling and/or better
compilers.  My thinking is that Digital would be doing very well to just
extract the same average performance level from each integer
unit even with sophisticated scheduling while keeping cycle time low.  



