The thread has lost coherence.  The Original debate was on the SPEC/MHz
rating of the 21264, it was slightly unclear whether the chip was going
to achieve the claimed 40 SPECInt95 score on a 400 MHz clock speed or
600 MHz clock speed.  If the speed was 600 MHz, then scaling to 1 GHz,
it was very unlikely that it would achieve the claimed 100 SpecInt95 
score at that speed.  The Die shrink and associated speed scaling were
all assuming the same 21264 core, not the 21364 or 21264x, with even more
parallel pipelines, or cache.  Just about the only improvement that could 
be achieved in the Spec/MHz rating would have to come from improved 
memory technology/interface (faster/bigger cache?) and/also better
optimizing compilers.   

No one has yet conclusively stated what the clock speed is for the 
claimed 40 SpecInt box. 400 or 600? 
