We were thinking of converting one of our Digital Personal Workstation
500au machines from Digital UNIX to Windows NT as a test bed for a 
possible general move towards NT.  Without getting into the desirability of
that general decision, I wonder if anyone has done any benchmarking of a
computational-intensive Fortran program running under Digital UNIX
(using Digital UNIX's Fortran 90 compiler) and running under Windows
NT (using Digital's DVF 90 compiler suite) on a PWS500au (or 433 or 600 MHz)
