Message-ID: <1998Feb5.103142.1242@flying-disk.spamblock.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 322412534
Organization: Flying Disk Systems, Inc.
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I am having a problem reading 4mm DAT tapes made on a DEC TLZ09,
using two different Archive Python 4322NP/4542NP drives.    I can
mount (/FOREIGN) the tapes OK and the volume label is displayed OK.
I do a BACKUP/LIST and the first 40-100 files are listed, then
it fails with excessive errors.

The TLZ09 is on our Alphaserver 1000A.   It is a replacement
for a series of TLZ07 drives which were failing at an alarming
rate.   It has now been a month since it was installed, with
zero errors or problems other than this compatibility issue.

The tapes are 3M (Imation) DDS-90.   These particular tapes
were first used in August 1997, and have been used about seven
times (BACKUP/VERIFY).

I have no problems writing tapes on the Archive drives and
reading them on the TLZ09.

Has anyone else experienced this problem?   Any ideas?

Also, what OEM drives did DEC use for the various TLZ0x models?

Did they ever use the Archive Python 4322NP/4542NP drives?

