In article <6ba9eb$os6$1@news.ccit.arizona.edu>, zaft@f1n7.u.arizona.edu (Gordon C Zaft) writes:
:1)	I have a TK50Z-GA that works fine with my VS3100/30.  Will it work
:with a MicroVAX 2000?  I know that there was a TK50Z-FA that worked with
:the 2000, but will the (presumably later ROM) -GA work also?  

  Probably.

  TK50Z-GA is a better choice, and the only choice for a VAXstation 3100
  series, but both the -FA and the -GA should work on a VAxstation 2000.

:2)	Is the interconnect cable used for the KA630 to MS630 the same or
:compatible with the interconnect for KA650 to MS650 and KA655 to MS650?

  I'd avoid it.

  I have heard of of folks that have run with the KA630 PMI cables
  successfully in a KA650, and I know of folks that have had problems
  with them -- I'd suspect it has to do with the version of the PMI cable
  and the phase of the moon.  (The PMI cable is sensitive to random
  interference -- and later cables tend to be more resistent.)   And
  of course the KA650 PMI cable provides for four (or five) connectors,
  for a total of 64 MB of memory (4 x 16 MB).  Personally, I remember
  having problems with the PMI configuration, until I got one of the
  KA650 PMI cables...

