> Not to take away from the 21264, it is very impressive to be talking of 1GHz
> clock rates in a "brainiac" out of order CPU.

I do not think that out-of-order necessarily implies brainiac.

For example, you could have a 1-wide out-of-order machine.
While more complicated than a in-order 1-wide machine, it is,
IMHO, less complicated, at least wrt the circuits that affect cycletime,
than an in-order superscalar machine of say, 3 or 4-wide.

Furthermore, good OOO microarchitecture reduces the circuit impact.
You don't have to choose stupid implementations for you OOO datastructures.

Anecdote: a friend of mine, used to work for me, was at the MICRO conference
 a few years back, and got into a discussion with an Alpha architect. The Digital
guy said "we used to think that OOO meant slow circuits - but the (Intel) P6 showed
us that this was not necessarily the case".





