References: <01bd2cf5$adcd3b40$83d609ce@jhawley> <6au1g2$rui$2@news.inc.net>
Organization: ColourCare International
Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec


Paul,
  Just done this myself funnily enough.
Firstly I use UCX 4.1 on VMS 6.2.

1. You have to ensure that both services BOOTP and TFTP are running on the
Vax
With UCX>  SHO SERVICE will show status.

2. The Decserver always tries MOP first so I had to change the Filename on
the Decserver from MMENG1 to another name (I used TCENG1)
The syntax was CHANGE SERVER SOFTWARE tceng1
(Note: After first load with IP this will become the default load method)

3.  Copied the file MMENG1.SYS from MOM$LOAD: directory to
UCX$TFTP_ROOT:tceng1.sys

4.  Created an entry in the BOOTP database for the Decserver.
With UCX> SET BOOTP decserverhostname /FILE=TCENG1.SYS -
/HARD=ADDR=decserverhardwareaddress /NETW=yoursubnetmask
i.e. set bootp decser1 /file=tceng1.sys /hard=addr=08-00-2b-xx-xx-xx
/netw=255.255.255.0
(Note: above example assumes the host decser1 is defined in the host
database)

Notes:
Assume that you have set the Decserver up correctly with CHANGE INTERNET
command
Need address, subnet mask, nameserver , host ( I think thats all !)
 
