In article <34D79952.CB2EB9FE@nastything.com>, Cyber Sidhe <cyber-sidhe@nastything.com> writes:
|> I am buying a DECstation/unix workstation 5000/200 and was wondering if
|> anybody new where I can find out any info on the internet about these?
|> I have tried digital's home site, but to no avail.
|> 
|> My questions are:  How easy are they to upgrade?, find parts for? are
|> they still being made? and what are your personal experiences with
|> them?  I appreciate any help that you can  offer:>

This is a very old system, and Digital hasn't manufactured these
in 6 or 7 years.  The codename for this system was "3MAX", so
an AltaVista search for "3max" might turn up additional information.

You can find some fairly detailed technical information in
	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/specs/
for the DECstation 5000/200, and for some of the older
TurboChannel interfaces that plug into its bus.

I don't think there is any way to upgrade the CPU, but you can
plug a fairly large amount of RAM into it (not standard PC RAM,
however!)  Depending on the operating system support, you can
probably use almost any decent SCSI disk.

The ULTRIX operating system is still officially supported on
this hardware, although there is little if any chance of a
