Bernhard H. Buckel <buckel@wmad95.mathematik.uni-wuerzburg.de> writes...
}I grabbed a cheap DEC LN03 laser printer this weekend. For the few bucks I
}had to spend on this, I didn't get any documentation along with it. I know
}that I can drive this beast with ghostscript under Linux but it barfs on me,
}showing the "red man" and an error code #4 :-( which means I'd have to call
}a DEC engineer but I'm sure that this is rather easy to fix. I only need to
}know where to look.
}				  Bernhard

From the "Installing and Using the LN03A" manual the error #4 with the little
man symbol's problem is "OPC Sync Mark" (and it does say the corrective action
is "Call DIGITAL Field Service").

The OPC is the organic photoconductor cartridge. It might help just to
replace that. Otherwise I would guess that you need to clean or replace
some sensor that looks at a "synch mark" on the OPC, which is normally
done by your friendly field service guy.

As for other errors associated with the repair guy icon, this is the list:
error   problem         corrective action
-----   --------        -----------------
1       fusing          call DIGITAL Field Service
2       optical system  call
3       both 1 and 2    call
4       OPC sync mark   call
5       both 1 and 4    call
6       both 2 and 4    call
7       1, 2, and 4     call
8       main motor      call
9       <there is no 9>
A       errors 2 and 8  call
B       1, 2, and 8     call
C,D,E   <there is no C, D, or E>
F       engine driver   call

--- Carl



