Is there a set of comparative benchmarks for different =

commercially available alpha 21164a systems?  Each
vendor quotes essentially identical SpecFP and SpecInt,
which I suspect were taken verbatim from DEC support
literature.

There is an extremely confusing, and I suspect inaccurate,
alpha review in the February 98 BYTE (p43).  The review
ostensibly compares a trio of systems based on  the
"smaller, lower-cost Alpha 21164PC chip", but I=92d swear one
of the described systems, the Aspen Durango II, is really based
on the 21164a, and there is a sidebar describing the "96-KB Level 2
cache".  The Durango outperformed the other two systems by about
30% in floating point, which surprised the author.

Are there good reasons, apart from a reviewer mixing 21164PC
and 21164a systems, for 30% performance differences
in CPU-intensive benchmarks -- different memory configurations,
etc.?  The effect of the L3 cache size is pretty well established
for SpecFP, but all the reviewed systems supposedly had
2 MB L3.



