No, nice try but no cigar. NT 5 is much more than a new major release of NT.In
coding terms it bears almost no relationship with NT 4. It is 15 million
lines of code larger than NT 4 to start off with. The inclusion of things
like Active Directory Services, HYDRA, New User interface, Support for Zero
Administration Client and in Digitals case 64 bit support make it unrecognisable
from NT 4.

This coupled with bad NT 5 beta test reports and that fact the MS had delayed
delivering Active Directory Services and a number of other features has caused
