In article <Pine.HPP.3.95.980130105016.13370N-100000@fennel.ca.boeing.com>, "Minh H. Cao" <mhc1587@fennel.ca.boeing.com> writes:
:I try to setup the cluster with separate system disk on each machine.

  This configuration is supported.  You will need to configure one or
  more of the supported VMScluster communications interconnects, such
  as NI, FDDI, imbedded DSSI, CI, or MC (Alpha).  MultiHost SCSI (Alpha)
  and KFQSA-based DSSI (VAX) require additional VMScluster communications
  interconnect(s).

:What should I do to setup the cluster on each machine and after that
:how can I cluster them all together.

  Without intending to sound rude, have you read through the VMScluster
  documentation in the OpenVMS manual set?  (The VMScluster documentation
  covers -- in detail -- the steps that are needed to consolidate the two
  security environments into one, to coalesce the standalone files into
  one set of common files, and to configure the necessary VMScluster
  parameters appropriately...)

  The number of steps involved here -- as well as the real possibility
  of site-specific configuration variations -- is rather more than what
  can be reasonably answered in a newsgroup.  (That's why there is a
  substantial manual on the management of VMScluster configurations!)

:All my machine are using Multinet TCP/IP .

  The IP package is not directly relevent -- the VMScluster protocols do
  not operate over IP or DECnet -- though you will want to check through
  the MultiNet documentation for information on VMScluster enviroments.

