In article <34D681F5.1260@unforgettable.com>, "JONAS K." <sonicfx@unforgettable.com> writes:

> Could someone suggest a CDR for alpha. given that native drivers and
> software exist for it?.

If you know of software, you more or less have to pick a model that software
can handle, as there is no standard for the SCSI control sequences to record.

I have used Infoserver for at least 4 years now, and I believe it is still
the only VMS method supported by any vendor.  You can no longer buy the
control box new, but there must be some on the used market.  It would be
conceptually straghtforward for the VMS developers to make burners work
directly from the Alpha, but getting DEC management to sign up for
supporting it would by more difficult.

There are freeware drivers you can modify if you are in a "do it yourself"
mood, but I don't think people would want to bet their business on such
arrangement (what if the person who modified the driver leaves?).

