We've been using the micro-timer kernel option on a twin-CPU 466MHz AS4100 
with DU4.0B without apparent problems for months. But when we built the kernel 
for some multi-CPU AS4000's - also DU4.0B - with the micro-timer option, this 
started crashing immediately. We told DEC service in early December but this 
seems to be working its way through the system. Anyone else had this problem 
and found a fix?

